:31,"embedded":true},{"title":"On *TechHQ*, we’ve written about how slime mold hit the headlines thanks to its ability to solve complex logistical problems","target":"https://techhq.com/2023/04/biocomputers-an-alternative-to-quantum-computing/","line":37},{"title":"a proxy for ripeness – for example, in gauging the firmness of apples","target":"https://techhq.com/2023/06/strawberries-and-ai-deep-learning-digests-flavor-and-food-waste/","line":39},{"title":"single largest organisms","target":"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/strange-but-true-largest-organism-is-fungus/","line":43},{"title":"https://t.co/QB6BMvAoIn","target":"https://t.co/QB6BMvAoIn","line":50},{"title":"@JT\\_bluebird1","target":"https://twitter.com/JT_bluebird1?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw","line":50},{"title":"October 9, 2023","target":"https://twitter.com/Pier_Complexity/status/1711475915153146123?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw","line":52},{"title":"Plant Wave","target":"https://plantwave.com/en-gb/","line":58},{"title":"Adamatzky’s breakthrough paper, *Towards fungal computer*","target":"https://royalsocietypublishing.org/doi/10.1098/rsfs.2018.0029","line":62},{"title":"Neuromarketing brainwaves capitalize on sales opportunities","target":"https://techhq.com/news/neuromarketing-brainwaves-capitalize-on-sales-opportunities/","line":64},{"title":"![","target":"https://techhq.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/TF-Intro-1.webp","line":72}],"metadata":{"title":"Fungal machines: building computers and sensors from nature","source":"https://techhq.com/news/fungal-machines-building-computers-and-sensors-from-nature/","author":["[[James Tyrrell]]"],"published":"2023-11-06","created":"2026-05-07","description":"Fungal machines open the door to building self-assembling, self-repairing, biodegradable computers for sensing human stress and much more.","tags":["#clippings"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:raw/Fungal machines building computers and sensors from nature.md#---frontmatter---": {